---
description: >-
  Every architecture label kind (group title, service title and edge label)
  written the six ways of spec #1368: plain markdown, a quoted markdown
  string, bare backticks, a code span in plain text, the common tags and a
  written \n. Only the quoted markdown string reads markdown; the bare
  backticks and the code span are drawn as written, the tags draw and \n
  breaks the line.
---
architecture-beta
  group g1(cloud)[group **bold** _ital_]
  group g2(cloud)["`group **bold** _ital_`"]
  group g3(cloud)[`group **bold** _ital_`]
  group g4(cloud)[group a `code` b]
  group g5(cloud)[group <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>next H<sub>2</sub>O]
  group g6(cloud)[group one\ntwo]
  service s1(server)[service **bold** _ital_] in g1
  service s2(database)["`service **bold** _ital_`"] in g2
  service s3(disk)[`service **bold** _ital_`] in g3
  service s4(internet)[service a `code` b] in g4
  service s5(server)[service <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>next H<sub>2</sub>O] in g5
  service s6(database)[service one\ntwo] in g6
  s1:R -[edge **bold** _ital_]- L:s2
  s2:R -["`edge **bold** _ital_`"]- L:s3
  s1:B -[`edge **bold** _ital_`]- T:s4
  s4:R -[edge a `code` b]- L:s5
  s5:R -[edge <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>next H<sub>2</sub>O]- L:s6
  s2:B -[edge one\ntwo]- T:s5
